---
import ContentLayout from "../layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import ReleaseDownload from "../components/data/ReleaseDownload.astro";
import CommandBlock from "../components/data/CommandBlock.astro";
import EvidenceLinks from "../components/data/EvidenceLinks.astro";
import { stable } from "../data/catalog";
import { installCommands as commands } from "../lib/install";
import { withBase } from "../lib/urls";
const asset = stable.assets[0];
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Make it part of your workflow."
  eyebrow={`Download / Stable v${stable.version}`}
  description="Get the official Linux amd64 package. Check your environment, verify the download, then choose how Radivine starts."
>
  <div class="download-layout">
    <ReleaseDownload />
    <article class="prose">
      <section aria-labelledby="requirements">
        <h2 id="requirements">Start with the right setup.</h2>
        <p>
          The primary tested desktop is{" "}
          <strong>Linux Mint 22.3 · Cinnamon X11 · Nemo · amd64</strong>. Ubuntu
          24.04 package installation was verified in a container; that does not
          certify every Ubuntu desktop.{" "}
          <a href={withBase("compatibility/")}>
            Check the full compatibility matrix
          </a>
          .
        </p>
        <p>
          The package declares <code>libc6 ≥ 2.34</code>,{" "}
          <code>libgcc-s1 ≥ 3.0</code>, <code>fonts-dejavu-core</code> and{" "}
          <code>libfontconfig1</code>. Recommended packages include Nemo,
          X11/OpenGL libraries, systemd and Noto fonts. A suitable graphical
          session is still needed.
        </p>
        <p>
          No ARM package, Windows/macOS installer, RPM, AppImage, Flatpak, Snap
          or hosted apt repository is offered here. Native Wayland wheel support
          is unavailable.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="verify">
        <h2 id="verify">01 / Download and verify.</h2>
        <p>
          Save the package and <a href={stable.checksumsUrl}>SHA256SUMS.txt</a>{" "}
          in the same directory, or use these commands with <code>curl</code>{" "}
          installed. Run the following steps from that directory.
        </p>
        <CommandBlock title="Download release files" code={commands.download} />
        <CommandBlock title="Verify SHA-256" code={commands.verify} />
        <p>
          Continue only when the package reports <strong>OK</strong>. If
          verification fails, do not install that file; download both files
          again from the versioned release page.
        </p>
        <CommandBlock title="Expected package SHA-256" code={asset.sha256} />
        <p>
          The SHA-256 above matches the published checksum file, GitHub asset
          digest, and a fresh download checked on {stable.verifiedOn}. It
          verifies agreement with the published bytes; it is not a signed
          provenance guarantee.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="install">
        <h2 id="install">02 / Install the package.</h2>
        <CommandBlock title="Install with apt" code={commands.install} />
        <p>
          <code>apt</code> resolves declared dependencies. The package includes
          the wheel daemon/CLI, Control Center, read-only viewer, conversion
          worker, user service units, desktop entry and Nemo’s{" "}
          <strong>Open in Radivine</strong> action.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="first-launch">
        <h2 id="first-launch">03 / Start on your terms.</h2>
        <p>
          Open <strong>Radivine Control Center</strong> from your application
          menu, or run:
        </p>
        <CommandBlock title="Open Control Center" code={commands.start} />
        <p>
          On Dashboard choose <strong>Start Daemon</strong>. Login startup is
          opt-in; enable it there if wanted. Closing Control Center leaves the
          daemon running. The conversion worker starts on demand; it does not
          need to be enabled as a permanent service.
        </p>
        <p>
          For a systemd user session, this alternative enables the wheel now and
          at login:
        </p>
        <CommandBlock title="Optional login startup" code={commands.service} />
        <p>
          Use these commands as your ordinary desktop user, without{" "}
          <code>sudo</code>. On a non-systemd desktop, Control Center has a
          fallback path, but that desktop still needs verification.{" "}
          <a href={withBase("guide/")}>Continue with the usage guide</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="upgrade">
        <h2 id="upgrade">Upgrade or remove.</h2>
        <p>
          Finish or cancel active jobs before restarting or removing services.
          Download and verify the new package first. For an existing
          systemd-managed installation:
        </p>
        <CommandBlock title="Upgrade and restart" code={commands.upgrade} />
        <p>
          The recorded v0.2.0 and release-candidate upgrades to v
          {stable.version} preserved user TOML and job history. Back up
          important configuration before changes; this is not a guarantee for
          every future migration. Non-systemd users can restart from Control
          Center.
        </p>
        <CommandBlock
          title="Remove a systemd-managed installation"
          code={commands.remove}
        />
        <p>
          For other startup methods, disable login startup and stop the daemon
          in Control Center before <code>sudo apt remove radivine</code>.
          Removal leaves user configuration and job history in your home
          directory. No command here deletes those files.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="source">
        <h2 id="source">Prefer to build from source?</h2>
        <p>
          The release CI reference toolchain is Rust <strong>1.95.0</strong>. A
          lower minimum is not established by the edition or older README
          wording. Install the C/build, graphical and packaging prerequisites in
          the{" "}
          <a
            href={`https://github.com/marawan6569/Radivine/blob/${stable.sourceRevision}/README.md`}
          >
            version-pinned source guide
          </a>
          .
        </p>
        <CommandBlock title="Build the pinned source" code={commands.source} />
        <p>
          A build alone does not install desktop entries, Nemo actions or
          services. The repository’s <code>./scripts/build-deb.sh</code> handles
          packaging and additionally needs Debian packaging tools and Python
          Pillow. This website does not claim to have repeated the full
          source-build installation on every distribution.
        </p>
        <EvidenceLinks
          ids={["packaging", "release-report", "cli", "release-live"]}
        />
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
  <nav class="page-links" aria-label="Release resources">
    <a href={stable.releaseUrl}>Release notes ↗</a>
    <a
      href={`https://github.com/marawan6569/Radivine/blob/${stable.sourceRevision}/CHANGELOG.md`}
    >
      Changelog ↗
    </a>
    <a href="https://github.com/marawan6569/Radivine/releases">
      Historical releases ↗
    </a>
    <a href={withBase("guide/troubleshooting/")}>Installation help →</a>
  </nav>
</ContentLayout>
<style>
  .download-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.4fr);
    gap: 4rem;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .prose section:first-child h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .download-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 3rem;
    }
  }
</style>
